# Kernel blocks

A kernel-vernacular document split into blocks exactly as the kernel's document
door splits it: a comment is a block (`-- …` to its line's end, `/- … -/`
nested), and a command ends at the first `.` outside a string and outside a
«quoted name» that is followed by whitespace or the end. So a block number here
is the block number the kernel reports, and a refused block can be shown back.

## Note
A document's blocks, or the reason it has none: an unterminated comment, which
the kernel refuses too.

## A Blocks has:
    an items, which is Seq of Text.
    a problem, which is Text.

## Note
Whether a byte is whitespace, and the byte at a 1-based position (0 past either end).

## To isSpaceByte (b: Int) -> Bool:
    Return b is equal to 32 or b is equal to 9 or b is equal to 10 or b is equal to 13.

## To byteAt (bs: Seq of Int, i: Int) -> Int:
    If i is less than 1 or i is greater than length of bs:
        Return 0.
    Return item i of bs.

## Note
The last byte of a block that starts at `i`, or `-1` for a comment never closed.

## To blockEnd (bs: Seq of Int, i: Int) -> Int:
    Let n be length of bs.
    Let mutable j be i.
    If byteAt(bs, i) is equal to 45 and byteAt(bs, i + 1) is equal to 45:
        While j is less than n and item j of bs is not equal to 10:
            Set j to j + 1.
        Return j.
    Let mutable depth be 0.
    If byteAt(bs, i) is equal to 47 and byteAt(bs, i + 1) is equal to 45:
        While j is less than n:
            Let pair be byteAt(bs, j) * 256 + byteAt(bs, j + 1).
            If pair is equal to 47 * 256 + 45:
                Set depth to depth + 1.
                Set j to j + 1.
            If pair is equal to 45 * 256 + 47:
                Set depth to depth - 1.
                Set j to j + 1.
                If depth is equal to 0:
                    Return j.
            Set j to j + 1.
        Return 0 - 1.
    Let mutable mode be 0.
    While j is at most n:
        Let b be item j of bs.
        If mode is equal to 2:
            Set mode to 1.
        Otherwise:
            If mode is equal to 3:
                If b is equal to 194 and byteAt(bs, j + 1) is equal to 187:
                    Set mode to 0.
            Otherwise:
                If b is equal to 34:
                    Set mode to 1 - mode.
                If mode is equal to 1 and b is equal to 92:
                    Set mode to 2.
                If mode is equal to 0 and b is equal to 194 and byteAt(bs, j + 1) is equal to 171:
                    Set mode to 3.
                If mode is equal to 0 and b is equal to 46 and (j is equal to n or isSpaceByte(byteAt(bs, j + 1))):
                    Return j.
        Set j to j + 1.
    Return n.

## Note
The blocks of a document, in order, each trimmed.

## To kernelBlocks (doc: Text) -> Blocks:
    Let bs be text_bytes(doc).
    Let mutable out be a new Seq of Text.
    Let mutable i be 1.
    While i is at most length of bs:
        If isSpaceByte(item i of bs):
            Set i to i + 1.
        Otherwise:
            Let last be blockEnd(bs, i).
            If last is less than 0:
                Return a new Blocks with items out and problem "an unterminated `/-` comment opens block {length of out + 1}".
            Push trim(text_from_bytes(items i through last of bs)) to out.
            Set i to last + 1.
    Return a new Blocks with items out and problem "".

## Note
The text of block `k` of a document, or the empty text.

## To blockText (doc: Text, k: Int) -> Text:
    Let blocks be (kernelBlocks(doc))'s items.
    If k is less than 1 or k is greater than length of blocks:
        Return "".
    Return item k of blocks.

## Test: a period inside a name or a string does not end a command

Let blocks be (kernelBlocks("Definition Lean.Eq.rec.{{u}} : Prop := True.\nCheck «a. b».\nEval \"x. y\"."))'s items.
Expect that blocks is equal to ["Definition Lean.Eq.rec.{{u}} : Prop := True.", "Check «a. b».", "Eval \"x. y\"."].

## Test: comments are blocks, nested ones whole, and an unclosed one is refused

Let ok be kernelBlocks("/- outer /- inner -/ still -/\n-- a note. with a period\nCheck Zero.").
Expect that ok's items is equal to ["/- outer /- inner -/ still -/", "-- a note. with a period", "Check Zero."].
Expect that (kernelBlocks("Check Zero.\n/- never closed"))'s problem is equal to "an unterminated `/-` comment opens block 2".
Expect that blockText("Check Zero.\n\nEval Zero.", 2) is equal to "Eval Zero.".

## Test: an escaped quote does not end a string

For all booleans escaped:
    Let mutable inner be "x".
    If escaped:
        Set inner to "x\\\". y".
    Expect that length of (kernelBlocks("Eval \"" + inner + "\".\nCheck Zero."))'s items is equal to 2.
